---
import PageLayout from '@micro/ui/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  site={site}
  title={`About | ${site.name}`}
  description="About the free online mic, webcam, keyboard and dead pixel tests: what they do and how they protect your privacy."
  path="/about/"
  heading="About Device Test"
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }]}
>
  <p>
    Device Test is a free set of simple checks for the hardware you use every day: your microphone, webcam, keyboard
    and screen. It is useful before a video call, after buying a new monitor or keyboard, or when something stops
    working and you want to know whether the problem is the device or an app.
  </p>
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mic test:</strong> live input level, device picker and an optional 5-second recording you can play back.</li>
    <li><strong>Webcam test:</strong> live preview, resolution and frame rate, mirror toggle and snapshots.</li>
    <li><strong>Keyboard test:</strong> on-screen ANSI or ISO layout that lights up each key you press.</li>
    <li><strong>Dead pixel test:</strong> full-screen solid colours to spot dead, stuck and hot pixels.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Privacy by design</h2>
  <p>
    All tests run in your browser. Audio and video never leave your device, there are no accounts, and the site’s
    security settings block connections to other servers. See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
  </p>
  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    A browser can only see what your operating system shares with it. These tests are a quick first check; they
    can’t diagnose every hardware fault. If you find a problem, please <a href="/contact/">let us know</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
